WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.620
It's great to welcome to the program today,
Stephen Kinzer, who's an author, journalist,

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.549
former New York times chorus

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:12.530
respondent. The newest book is poisoner in
chief Sydney Gottlieb and the CIA search for

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.170
mind control. Steven, so great to have you
on,

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.910
good to be with you.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.560
So there are a lot of these buzzwords that
will often trigger a lot of conspiratorial

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:29.520
thinking, but that often have a real story
behind them that is not as nefarious as some

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.809
make it out to be, but still worthy of discussion.
So the build the bird group is one that is

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:42.320
often under this umbrella area. 51 is another
example, uh, MK ultra. I would also consider

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.859
one of those where if you do a cursory internet
search, you will find a lot of crazy stuff,

00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:51.850
but it is a real program that existed. So
where do we start? What's, what's the best

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.129
way to kind of start our, our understanding
of what this was?

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:02.920
So this is my 10th book and I've tried to
devote myself over my career to trying to

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:10.530
figure out a little bit of what goes on behind
the facade of, uh, public politics and public

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:15.079
diplomacy that we can see in the course of
my research. I've come up with a lot of things

00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:19.820
that are surprising and some things that may
have shocked some people, but this is the

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:28.409
first time I've been shot. I still can't believe
that this project MK ultra was as intense

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:34.729
and horrific as it was. And I can't believe
that this unknown figure Sydney Gottlieb actually

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:41.560
existed. So my book is an attempt essentially
to write the biography of a guy who in many

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:48.060
ways wasn't there. He was even within the
CIA, almost completely unknown in terms of

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:55.469
what he was actually doing. MK ultra was a
real program. It lasted for some 10 years.

00:01:55.469 --> 00:02:05.049
It was aimed at finding the secret of mind
control. And in pursuit of that secret, Sidney

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:12.780
Goglia who became the chief chemist of the
CIA, uh, carried out the most extreme experiments

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:19.750
on human subjects that have ever been carried
out by any agency or officer of the U S government.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:30.160
He had concluded that before you could figure
out how to insert a new mine into somebody's

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:36.440
brain, you first had to find a way to blast
away the mind that was in there. And he spent

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:42.240
10 years working on combinations of drugs,
electroshock and all kinds of other techniques

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:48.500
aimed at finding ways to destroy a human mind
and a human body in a human soul.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:56.880
Did this start, uh, sort of in response to
the belief that, uh, Russia already had figured

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.880
out how to do this and that the U S was behind
in a sense, what was the role of the cold

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:06.430
war in, in sort of triggering or fomenting
this project?

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:10.650
You can't understand this project without
understanding the era. So in the early days

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:17.060
of the cold war, Americans were made to believe
that we had this horrific enemy that was plotting

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:23.450
our liquidation day and night. If you bought
into that, as most Americans did, it would

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:29.650
seem that any defensive mechanism would be
justified. The loss of a few lives or even

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:35.380
a few hundred lives would seem like a a tiny
price to pay. Now, there were a couple of

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:44.280
particular incidents that led the CIA to conclude
that indeed the communists, as we called them,

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:50.470
I had discovered the secret to mind control.
One of them was the trial of the Roman Catholic

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:56.090
prelate of Hungary, cargo woman Senti. Um,
he was put on trial by a communist authorities

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:03.000
and, uh, he seemed to be speaking in a monotone
with glazed eyes as he confessed to crimes

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.430
that he obviously hadn't committed.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:10.320
Later on, it turned out that he had been coerced
with the normal techniques that interrogators

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:15.209
use, like extended isolations and beatings
and repeated interrogation. But we didn't

00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:21.500
see it that way. The CIA thought, ah, he has
been brainwashed and somehow the communists

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:28.350
are controlling what he's saying. The other
episode came after the Korean war when it

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:34.410
turned out that not only had a number of American
prisoners signed statements denouncing the

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:39.350
United States or even confessing to war crimes,
but a number of them decided they wanted to

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:45.390
stay behind and they would rather live under
a communist society and then come back to

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:51.170
America. This was interpreted also at the
CIA as something that only could have become

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:57.971
possible if they had been brainwashed. So
I asked myself a second question though. What

00:04:57.971 --> 00:05:07.270
was it that led CIA officers to embrace this
fantasy of mind control a and re and misinterpret

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:13.150
these incidents? I think maybe it had to do
with the books and stories and movies that

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:17.870
these people had ingested it as they grew
up. There are all kinds of Sherlock Holmes

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:25.360
stories and Edgar Allen Poe's stories and
movies like Svengali and Gaslight. I think

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:32.270
they created a kind of a fertile mind, uh,
in the CIA that led them to be willing to

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:37.600
believe something that even Sydney got leave
himself after 10 years of destroying human

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.810
lives. Realized it was a myth.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:46.500
What was the role of, uh, the hallucinogenic
LSD and all of this? Was LSD mixed in as possibly

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:53.610
a tool to be used or was it misunderstood
and actually had nothing to do with this?

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:59.870
Sydney godly? The director of MK ultra was
fascinated with LSD. He and his fellow chemists

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:05.050
believed that it might be, as one of them
put it, the key that could unlock the universe.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:11.060
He thought this might be the mind control
drug. He himself by his own account, used

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:20.410
LSD more than 200 times. So in 1953, Sydney
godly persuaded the CIA to buy the entire

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:26.550
world's supply of LSD. He brought it from
Switzerland to the United States and he used

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:33.860
it for two purposes. One was in horrific experiments
in American prisons and it's secret detention

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:40.270
centers around the world. And then there was
another piece, he also used it for non-coercive

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:45.680
experiments on volunteers who were actually
told that they were taking a psychoactive

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:52.270
substance. And this leads to one of God lives
most unexpected legacies. So through a couple

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:58.870
of bogus medical foundations that he established
a Gottlieb, sent LSD to dozens of clinics

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:05.780
and hospitals and universities around the
country, uh, and paid them to call for volunteers

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:13.210
that would be paid a small amount and take
LSD who were among the first people who volunteered.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:19.020
One of them was Ken Keasy who went onto write
one flew over the Cuckoo's nest. He loved

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:24.541
LSD so much did he actually took a job in
the hospital in Menlo park, California, so

00:07:24.541 --> 00:07:30.280
he could steal the LSD out of the medicine
chest and bring it home to his friends. Another

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:36.580
one was the poet Alan Ginsburg, who took it
at a CIA sponsored experiment at Stanford.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:42.410
Of course, not knowing that it was CIA sponsored,
another was Robert Hunter, the lyricist for

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:48.180
the grateful dead, who introduced LSD to the
other members of the band. So it was through

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:55.810
God leave and MK ultra that LSD leaped out
of the laboratory into the general population.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:08:02.220
And of course, the irony is the drug that
Gottlieb thought might give the CIA the tool

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:08.270
to control people's minds actually wound up
fueling a generational rebellion. That was

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:11.620
aimed at destroying everything as the, I believe.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:18.770
So you mentioned experiments, horrible experiments.
What types of things are we talking about?

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:23.729
Godly conducted experiments in the United
States and outside the United States. Inside

00:08:23.729 --> 00:08:30.340
the U S his favorite subjects were prisoners
for obvious reasons. Um, for example, I came

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:37.610
across one experiment that was carried out
at the federal prison in Kentucky. Seven African

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:43.269
American inmates were segregated into a cell.
And without being told what was happening

00:08:43.269 --> 00:08:53.029
to them, we're given triple doses of LSD every
day for 77 days. So this was a way for godly

00:08:53.029 --> 00:08:57.570
to try to figure out if you could destroy
a mind with this kind of an overdose. And

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:03.959
actually of course, the answer is yes, you
can. Um, abroad God leaves experiments were

00:09:03.959 --> 00:09:10.970
even more intense. Um, as he started out on
the project, godly as a good scientist asked

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:16.379
himself what research is already out there?
Who are the experts that exist on how to destroy

00:09:16.379 --> 00:09:18.829
a human mind and the human body?

00:09:18.829 --> 00:09:24.750
So the first obvious answer was the Nazi doctors
who had worked in the concentration cares

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:32.491
and the CIA hired Nazi doctors. Not only to
help design these so-called experiments, but

00:09:32.491 --> 00:09:39.149
to help oversee them. Uh, I visited in the
course of research for this book, what I think

00:09:39.149 --> 00:09:46.319
maybe the very first CIA secret prison. It's
in a lovely chalet outside Frankfurt in Germany.

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:50.730
Uh, the young German businessman who now owns
that house. It was nice enough to take me

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:57.449
into the basement and he showed me his storage
rooms and told me these were the cells where

00:09:57.449 --> 00:10:03.850
the CIA scientists and their Nazi partners
conducted these extreme experiments, which

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:09.910
were essentially just continuations of the
experiments that the Nazis had been carrying

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:16.209
out just a few years ago in the concentration
camps right down the road. So who were the

00:10:16.209 --> 00:10:22.519
victims in these subjects and these experiments?
Um, they were people that the CIA charmingly

00:10:22.519 --> 00:10:25.040
described as Expendables.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:32.249
Um, people who, uh, if they died, nobody would
miss so suspected enemy agents who had been

00:10:32.249 --> 00:10:39.769
captured refugees who didn't seem to be connected
to anybody in East Asia. A number of the subjects

00:10:39.769 --> 00:10:46.649
were captured North Korean prisoners of war.
People for home, there would be no, as they

00:10:46.649 --> 00:10:53.709
called it, disposal problem. And the guy who
actually owns this former CIA torture house

00:10:53.709 --> 00:11:00.499
told me that, uh, older people in the neighborhood
all know what happened in this house. And

00:11:00.499 --> 00:11:05.490
in fact, I just found an article in dare Spiegel
that German magazines saying this was the

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:10.999
CIA torture house. There were deaths, but
the number is unknown. And this guy tells

00:11:10.999 --> 00:11:17.819
me these older people around here, I've told
me the victims who died, who were experimented

00:11:17.819 --> 00:11:23.439
to death were buried in the forests around
here in places that are now covered up by

00:11:23.439 --> 00:11:25.920
shopping malls and apartment blocks.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:30.579
So in the limited time we have left two questions.
One, what ultimately led to the end of this

00:11:30.579 --> 00:11:36.230
program? And number two, at the time the program
was going on, I, I presume that it was classified

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:40.920
when was anything public first known about
the program.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:48.959
So MK ultra did not come to a sharp end, petered
out in the early 1960s and Sydney godly, uh,

00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:55.209
who, although he was his generation's most
prolific torturer, um, was also a scientist,

00:11:55.209 --> 00:12:00.410
was forced to conclude. In the end that mind
control doesn't exist. You cannot persuade

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:07.209
somebody or make somebody commit murder, for
example, if that is deeply against committing

00:12:07.209 --> 00:12:13.600
murder. It's just a made up fantasy. Gottlieb
had to admit this. And uh, that led to the

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:20.360
end of MK ultra after 10 years of laying waste
to unknown numbers of human lives. It wasn't

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:28.100
until the mid 1970s. So another 15 years after
the program ended that the first pieces of

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:34.949
information began to leak out. That was when
a few people, uh, who had been got leaves

00:12:34.949 --> 00:12:42.269
victims slowly began to understand what might've
happened to them. But on the way out of the

00:12:42.269 --> 00:12:50.579
CIA, when he retired in 1973, godly, destroyed
almost all of the records of MK ultra. So

00:12:50.579 --> 00:12:57.589
in my work putting together this book, I've
had to piece together a whole variety of sources.

00:12:57.589 --> 00:13:02.600
And at the end of the book, I have a line,
which maybe is my favorite line in the book.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:08.619
I write a, everything in this book is true,
but not everything that's true is in this

00:13:08.619 --> 00:13:16.339
book. I'm painfully aware that I only discovered
a portion of what MK ultra was and who Sidney

00:13:16.339 --> 00:13:21.119
Gottlieb was. But a, it's certainly as far
as anybody's managed to get up to now,

00:13:21.119 --> 00:13:26.239
we have been talking about Stephen Kinzer,
his book poisoner in chief Sydney Gottlieb

00:13:26.239 --> 00:13:32.019
and the CIA search for mind control. Steven
is an author, a journalist, and former New

00:13:32.019 --> 00:13:33.019
York

00:13:33.019 --> 00:13:36.449
times correspondent. Steven, thank you so
much for talking to us about the book. That

00:13:36.449 --> 00:13:37.250
was great.

